<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Lemma.app and the three sidecars Tauri signs with it: lemma-locald,
     lemma-agent-host and lemma-runtime.

     Empty on purpose. Tauri 2 has one entitlements setting per build and
     applies it to every target it signs (the frameworks, each externalBin,
     then the bundle), so anything written here is granted to all four. None of
     them can use com.apple.security.virtualization: only lemma-vz links
     Virtualization.framework, and it carries the entitlement in its own
     signature. See lemma-vz.entitlements.plist.

     Nothing else is needed either. The app is not sandboxed, so network access
     needs no entitlement; WKWebView's JIT runs in the system's own WebContent
     process, under Apple's signature and not this one; and every executable
     Lemma starts (python, node, the guest helper) is a separate process
     evaluated on its own signature.

     A grant added here is a grant to the process that hosts a WebView. Put it
     in the signature of the thing that needs it instead.
     scripts/check_entitlements.py enforces exactly that. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
